# The Four Basic Database Operations :
 Almost every application needs to perform four fundamental operations. We call them CRUD : Create, Read, Update and Delete.

* Application = logic
* Database = persistent data
* API = communication between application components
* CRUD = basic operations performed on data

# ACID
 is an acronym for the four major properties of a database transaction: Atomicity , consistency , isolation , Durability.

* Atomicity : all or nothing treating transaction as a single unit
* Consistency : data remains constant according to the defined rule before and after transaction 
* Isolation : Cooncurrent transaction dont interfere with each other
* Durability : onse the transaction is commited , it presists even after system failure 

# Relational Database : 
stores data in the form of tables and establishes relationships between those tables.

# SQL : 
Structured Query Language is a language used to communicate with relational databases. eg SELECT * FROM users; // give all record form student table 

# Table :
   Collection of row and column (complete Structure) eg. students
* Column : A property attribute
* Row : one complete record 

# Primary Key : 
A primary key is a column, or combination of columns, used to uniquely identify each record in a table.It should be unique, not null and stable enough to identify the record. Mostly we use id as primary key . eg Stuent_id in student table 

# Foreign Key : 
A foreign key is used to establish a relationship between tables.

# Types Of Relationships
* One-to-One : One record relates to one record. eg. one person has one passport.
* One-to-Many : One record relates to many records. eg. one user can have many tasks.
* Many-to-Many : Many records relate to many records.eg. one student can take many courses and one coures can have many students.

# Normalization
Normalization is the process of organizing data to reduce unnecessary duplication and improve data integrity.The goal is to Store each piece of information in an appropriate place and connect it through relationships. eg if a department is changed we may need to change it in multiple tables if it was normalized changing at one table changes all data .

